            <div xml:id="d227">

                <pb facs="0709" n="695" xml:id="pg695"/>

                <head><seg type="margin">[671]</seg> *<hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Preston, Secretary of the Navy, to Commodore
                            Parker, commanding home
                    squadron.</hi></head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Navy Department</hi></placeName>,
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1850-05-15"><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >May</hi> 15, 1850</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The confidential instructions, in relation
                    to which I conferred with you this morning, are being prepared, and will be
                    dispatched by to-morrow’s mail.</p>
                <p>As there is no vessel of the home squadron within your reach, I have not deemed
                    it necessary to order you to proceed to the scene of action, and particularly as
                    the condition of your family is such as to render it somewhat inconvenient to
                    you.</p>
                <p>The Saranac will proceed forthwith.</p>
                <p>I am, very respectfully, yours, &amp;c., &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>WILLIAM B. PEESTON.</item>
                            <item>Commodore <hi rendition="#small-caps">F. A. Parker</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Commanding Home Squadron, Washington, D.
                                    C.</hi></item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
